      "timestamp": "1970-01-01T00:00:00+00:00",
      "text": "Classical control probe rejected \u2014 no pure-classical fallback accepted\nThe forced classical-only control probe did not negotiate. When the hybrid probe succeeded, this is a positive hardening signal: the server offers no pure-classical downgrade path. Readiness is deliberately NOT_APPLICABLE \u2014 it never overrides the hybrid or legacy-protocol axes, which are the actual readiness signal; this finding only records that the control probe itself was rejected (issue #232 \u2014 this was previously misattributed to tls.hybrid.probe_failed, incorrectly turning a successful hybrid scan into a reported failure)."
